{"base_rate":0.16666666666666666,"brier":0.07506957928802588,"bss":0.45949902912621365,"bss_hi":0.5382804447148163,"bss_lo":0.37033139514081426,"chart":{"base":[278.1,51.7],"fp":[216.3,363.4],"lead":"62,266.2 272,247 482,214.7 692,164.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.46 — higher than 85% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end +1pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 74% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 62% → rained 63%"},"rel":"62,461.9 118.2,414.5 451.2,195.1"},"country":"IR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.015307443365695762,"ess":338.5271125176309,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Tabriz</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Tabriz rain forecast is genuinely useful, and honest except at one point on the scale.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (81%), believe about\n<b>81%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 618 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-02-27. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 1.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.46, ranked 31 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(13&ndash;70) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>316</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>112</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>17%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>81%</td><td class='num'><b>81%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">1 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Tabriz</b> <span class=\"muted\">Iran</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">honest except at one point</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.46</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>13&ndash;70\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>618 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Tabriz &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Tabriz\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 72.95017857142858,352.75 118.733125,285.3125 212.321875,177.25 343.0841935483872,53.225806451612925 343.0841935483872,123.67741935483872 212.321875,268.25 118.733125,353.5625 72.95017857142858,378.75 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"321.3333333333333\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"321.3333333333333\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,378.54430379746833 72.95017857142858,352.75 118.733125,313.75 212.321875,217.0625 343.0841935483872,88.45161290322585\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 316 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"378.54430379746833\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 112 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"72.95017857142858\" cy=\"352.75\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 17%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"118.733125\" cy=\"313.75\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 44%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"212.321875\" cy=\"217.0625\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 81%&amp;#10;It rained 81% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 62 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"343.0841935483872\" cy=\"88.45161290322585\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(17%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Tabriz the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.48) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (0.39).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>128</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.387</td><td class='num'>3.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>172</td><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'>0.405</td><td class='num'>2.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>162</td><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'>0.418</td><td class='num'>0.8%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>156</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.482</td><td class='num'>2.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":38.08,"lon":46.2919,"n":618,"n_cities":213,"name":"Tabriz","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":316,"obs":0.00949367088607595,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.04223214285714287,"n":112,"obs":0.08035714285714286,"sig":false},{"hi":0.33,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.1715625,"n":64,"obs":0.1875,"sig":false},{"hi":0.609000000000002,"lo":0.33,"mean":0.43593750000000003,"n":64,"obs":0.453125,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.609000000000002,"mean":0.8053225806451615,"n":62,"obs":0.8064516129032258,"sig":false}],"prcp_km":1.0,"provisional":false,"rank":31,"rank_hi":70.0,"rank_lo":12.950000000000003,"reliability":0.0003665312215473984,"resolution":0.06358937585253582,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"tabriz","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Tehran"}